{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5337-1","published":"2026-11-17T19:02:21Z","modified":"2026-11-18T19:45:05.221725909Z","related":["CVE-2026-104029","CVE-2026-104031","CVE-2026-104032","CVE-2026-104033","CVE-2026-104035","CVE-2026-104036","CVE-2026-104037","CVE-2026-104039","CVE-2026-104041","CVE-2026-104042","CVE-2026-104043","CVE-2026-104045","CVE-2026-104048","CVE-2026-68742","CVE-2026-68744","CVE-2026-80048","CVE-2026-88252","CVE-2026-90462","CVE-2026-90463","CVE-2026-90994","CVE-2026-90995","CVE-2026-90996","CVE-2026-92821"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-104029","CVE-2026-104031","CVE-2026-104032","CVE-2026-104033","CVE-2026-104035","CVE-2026-104036","CVE-2026-104037","CVE-2026-104039","CVE-2026-104041","CVE-2026-104042","CVE-2026-104043","CVE-2026-104045","CVE-2026-104048","CVE-2026-68742","CVE-2026-68744","CVE-2026-80048","CVE-2026-88252","CVE-2026-90462","CVE-2026-90463","CVE-2026-90994","CVE-2026-90995","CVE-2026-90996","CVE-2026-92821"],"summary":"Security update for sssd","details":"This update for sssd fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-68742: heap out-of-bounds read due to unvalidated address lengths in NSS responder packet parsing\n  (bsc#1273922).\n- CVE-2026-68744: heap memory disclosure due to unshrunk packet allocations during group resolution (bsc#1273924).\n- CVE-2026-80048: `sssd-kcm`: local denial of service due to excessive memory preallocation (bsc#1284466).\n- CVE-2026-88252: denial of service via responder connection retry loop during file descriptor exhaustion\n  (bsc#1284465). \n- CVE-2026-90462: fail-open in LDAP `ppolicy` access check allows continued authorization for deleted user\n  (bsc#1282584).\n- CVE-2026-90463: out-of-bounds read in the NSS service request parsers (bsc#1280360).\n- CVE-2026-90994: out-of-bounds read in PAM v1 parser (bsc#1280361).\n- CVE-2026-90995: NULL pointer dereference in PAM responder (bsc#1280362).\n- CVE-2026-90996: zero-length request body underflow in the NSS responder (bsc#1280363).\n- CVE-2026-92821: access control bypass due to premature LDAP access rule evaluation (bsc#1284326).\n- CVE-2026-104029: denial of service due to out-of-bounds read in `autofs` responder (bsc#1284314).\n- CVE-2026-104031: denial of service via memory exhaustion in `autofs` responder (bsc#1284316).\n- CVE-2026-104032: denial of service via unprivileged `autofs` cache invalidation (bsc#1284317).\n- CVE-2026-104033: access control bypass due to improper LDAP shadow expiration check (bsc#1284318).\n- CVE-2026-104035: denial of service via memory exhaustion in KCM responder (bsc#1284320).  \n- CVE-2026-104036: denial of service due to out-of-bounds write in NFS `idmap` plugin (bsc#1284321).\n- CVE-2026-104037: denial of service due to packet length underflow in `autofs` responder (bsc#1284322).\n- CVE-2026-104039: denial of service due to stale connection state reuse in PAM GSSAPI responder (bsc#1284324).\n- CVE-2026-104041: denial of service via unbounded negative cache growth (bsc#1284254).\n- CVE-2026-104042: denial of service via out-of-bounds read in PAM responder (bsc#1284265).\n- CVE-2026-104043: denial of service via undersized packet parsing in NSS responder (bsc#1284266).\n- CVE-2026-104045: denial of service via race condition in `autofs` responder (bsc#1284470).\n- CVE-2026-104048: authorization bypass via cross-domain username collision in HBAC evaluation (bsc#1284467).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"sssd","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/sssd&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libsss_certmap0":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","libsss_idmap0":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","libsss_nss_idmap0":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","python3-sssd-config":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","sssd":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","sssd-ad":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","sssd-common":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","sssd-dbus":"2.5.2-150500.10.54.1","sssd-krb5":